questions.explanation:
Energy of one photon $= {{hc} \over \lambda }$ ($\lambda$ = 300 nm)

For one mole photons, $E = {{hc} \over \lambda } \times {N_A} E = {{6.626 \times {{10}^{ - 34}} \times 3 \times {{10}^8} \times 6.023 \times {{10}^{23}}} \over {300 \times {{10}^{ - 9}}}} E = 3.99 \times {10^5}$ J mol^{ - 1}

Kinetic energy $= 1.68 \times {10^5}$ J mol^{ - 1}

{W_0} = E - K.E. = 3.99 \times {10^5} - 1.68 \times {10^5} = 2.31 \times {10^5}$ J mol^{$-$1}

